<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tagsatzung</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">until 1848</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Federal Diet of Switzerland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tagsatzung, or Federal Diet, was the assembly of envoys of the cantons of the Old Swiss Confederacy and its successors until 1848. Delegates met in turn in various towns, bound by instructions from their cantons, and decisions needed the members' agreement, so its powers were limited. It handled common affairs such as the shared subject lands, war and foreign relations, and was replaced by the Federal Assembly under the constitution of 1848.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tagsatzung.jpg" alt="Tagsatzung" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tagsatzung1531.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
